{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Z/12: the integers mod 12 = 2^2 * 3\n  12 elements, characteristic 12\n  a field: no; an integral domain: no (12 is not prime: 2 * 6 = 0 with both nonzero)\n  CRT: Z/12 = Z/4 x Z/3 (a -> (a mod 4, a mod 3))\n  units: phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11\n  unit group: C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root\n  zero divisors: 7 nonzero (every nonzero non-unit of a finite ring): 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(12) = 6, 2 of them: 0, 6\n  idempotents: 2^2 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1, 4, 9\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 12 (6 of them; Z/12 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (2) (3) (4) (6) (0)\n  quotients: Z/12 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n  maximal = prime ideals: (2), (3) (quotients Z/p, fields)\n  check: by brute force over the 12 elements: 4 units, 7 zero divisors, 2 nilpotents, 4 idempotents\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring Z/12", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "a_field": "no; an integral domain: no (12 is not prime: 2 * 6 = 0 with both nonzero)", "crt": "Z/12 = Z/4 x Z/3 (a -> (a mod 4, a mod 3))", "units": "phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11", "unit_group": "C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root", "zero_divisors": "7 nonzero (every nonzero non-unit of a finite ring): 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10", "nilpotents": "the multiples of rad(12) = 6, 2 of them: 0, 6", "idempotents": "2^2 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1, 4, 9", "ideals": "(d) for each d | 12 (6 of them; Z/12 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (2) (3) (4) (6) (0)", "quotients": "Z/12 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)", "maximal": "prime ideals: (2), (3) (quotients Z/p, fields)", "lhs": "Z/12: the integers mod 12", "value": "2^2 * 3", "headline": "Z/12: the integers mod 12 = 2^2 * 3", "details": ["12 elements, characteristic 12"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "by brute force over the 12 elements: 4 units, 7 zero divisors, 2 nilpotents, 4 idempotents"}], "files": [], "text": "Z/12: the integers mod 12 = 2^2 * 3\n  12 elements, characteristic 12\n  a field: no; an integral domain: no (12 is not prime: 2 * 6 = 0 with both nonzero)\n  CRT: Z/12 = Z/4 x Z/3 (a -> (a mod 4, a mod 3))\n  units: phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11\n  unit group: C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root\n  zero divisors: 7 nonzero (every nonzero non-unit of a finite ring): 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(12) = 6, 2 of them: 0, 6\n  idempotents: 2^2 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1, 4, 9\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 12 (6 of them; Z/12 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (2) (3) (4) (6) (0)\n  quotients: Z/12 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n  maximal = prime ideals: (2), (3) (quotients Z/p, fields)\n  check: by brute force over the 12 elements: 4 units, 7 zero divisors, 2 nilpotents, 4 idempotents\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Z/1: the integers mod 1\n  1 elements, characteristic 1\n  the zero ring (0 = 1): not a field, not an integral domain\n  units: phi(1) = 1: 0\n  unit group: trivial (order 1, exponent lambda(1) = 1)\n  zero divisors: none besides 0\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(1) = 1, 1 of them: 0\n  idempotents: 2^0 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 1 (1 of them; Z/1 is a principal ideal ring): (0)\n  quotients: Z/1 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring Z/1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "units": "phi(1) = 1: 0", "unit_group": "trivial (order 1, exponent lambda(1) = 1)", "zero_divisors": "none besides 0", "nilpotents": "the multiples of rad(1) = 1, 1 of them: 0", "idempotents": "2^0 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0", "ideals": "(d) for each d | 1 (1 of them; Z/1 is a principal ideal ring): (0)", "quotients": "Z/1 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)", "headline": "Z/1: the integers mod 1", "details": ["1 elements, characteristic 1", "the zero ring (0 = 1): not a field, not an integral domain"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "Z/1: the integers mod 1\n  1 elements, characteristic 1\n  the zero ring (0 = 1): not a field, not an integral domain\n  units: phi(1) = 1: 0\n  unit group: trivial (order 1, exponent lambda(1) = 1)\n  zero divisors: none besides 0\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(1) = 1, 1 of them: 0\n  idempotents: 2^0 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 1 (1 of them; Z/1 is a principal ideal ring): (0)\n  quotients: Z/1 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Z/2: the integers mod 2\n  2 elements, characteristic 2\n  a field: yes (2 is prime: every nonzero a has an inverse, a^(2-2)); so also an integral domain\n  units: phi(2) = 1: 1\n  unit group: trivial (order 1, exponent lambda(2) = 1)\n  zero divisors: none besides 0\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(2) = 2, 1 of them: 0\n  idempotents: 2^1 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 2 (2 of them; Z/2 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (0)\n  quotients: Z/2 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n  maximal = prime ideals: (2) (quotients Z/p, fields)\n  check: by brute force over the 2 elements: 1 units, 0 zero divisors, 1 nilpotents, 2 idempotents\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring Z/2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "a_field": "yes (2 is prime: every nonzero a has an inverse, a^(2-2)); so also an integral domain", "units": "phi(2) = 1: 1", "unit_group": "trivial (order 1, exponent lambda(2) = 1)", "zero_divisors": "none besides 0", "nilpotents": "the multiples of rad(2) = 2, 1 of them: 0", "idempotents": "2^1 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1", "ideals": "(d) for each d | 2 (2 of them; Z/2 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (0)", "quotients": "Z/2 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)", "maximal": "prime ideals: (2) (quotients Z/p, fields)", "headline": "Z/2: the integers mod 2", "details": ["2 elements, characteristic 2"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "by brute force over the 2 elements: 1 units, 0 zero divisors, 1 nilpotents, 2 idempotents"}], "files": [], "text": "Z/2: the integers mod 2\n  2 elements, characteristic 2\n  a field: yes (2 is prime: every nonzero a has an inverse, a^(2-2)); so also an integral domain\n  units: phi(2) = 1: 1\n  unit group: trivial (order 1, exponent lambda(2) = 1)\n  zero divisors: none besides 0\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(2) = 2, 1 of them: 0\n  idempotents: 2^1 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 2 (2 of them; Z/2 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (0)\n  quotients: Z/2 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n  maximal = prime ideals: (2) (quotients Z/p, fields)\n  check: by brute force over the 2 elements: 1 units, 0 zero divisors, 1 nilpotents, 2 idempotents\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "GF(2^8) = GF(2)[x]/(x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1), 0x11d\n  256 elements (2^8), characteristic 2, dimension 8 over GF(2)\n  modulus: the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 8 over GF(2) (by its coefficients read as a base-2 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)\n  a field: yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(2^8) = x mod f and gcd(x^(2^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)\n  check by brute force over all 256 x 256 products: every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add\n  x has order 255: the modulus is primitive\n  unit group: cyclic of order 255 = 3 * 5 * 17; phi(255) = 128 generators\n  subfields: GF(2), GF(2^2), GF(2^4), GF(2^8) (GF(2^d) for each d | 8: the a with a^(2^d) = a)\n  Frobenius a -> a^2: an automorphism of order 8 fixing GF(2); the Galois group is cyclic of order 8\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring GF(2^8)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "modulus": "the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 8 over GF(2) (by its coefficients read as a base-2 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)", "a_field": "yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(2^8) = x mod f and gcd(x^(2^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8)", "x_has_order_255": "the modulus is primitive", "unit_group": "cyclic of order 255 = 3 * 5 * 17; phi(255) = 128 generators", "subfields": "GF(2), GF(2^2), GF(2^4), GF(2^8) (GF(2^d) for each d | 8: the a with a^(2^d) = a)", "lhs": "GF(2^8)", "value": "GF(2)[x]/(x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1), 0x11d", "headline": "GF(2^8) = GF(2)[x]/(x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1), 0x11d", "details": ["256 elements (2^8), characteristic 2, dimension 8 over GF(2)", "check by brute force over all 256 x 256 products: every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add", "Frobenius a -> a^2: an automorphism of order 8 fixing GF(2); the Galois group is cyclic of order 8"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)"}], "files": [], "text": "GF(2^8) = GF(2)[x]/(x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1), 0x11d\n  256 elements (2^8), characteristic 2, dimension 8 over GF(2)\n  modulus: the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 8 over GF(2) (by its coefficients read as a base-2 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)\n  a field: yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(2^8) = x mod f and gcd(x^(2^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)\n  check by brute force over all 256 x 256 products: every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add\n  x has order 255: the modulus is primitive\n  unit group: cyclic of order 255 = 3 * 5 * 17; phi(255) = 128 generators\n  subfields: GF(2), GF(2^2), GF(2^4), GF(2^8) (GF(2^d) for each d | 8: the a with a^(2^d) = a)\n  Frobenius a -> a^2: an automorphism of order 8 fixing GF(2); the Galois group is cyclic of order 8\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "GF(2^2) = GF(2)[x]/(x^2 + x + 1), 0x7\n  4 elements (2^2), characteristic 2, dimension 2 over GF(2)\n  modulus: the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 2 over GF(2) (by its coefficients read as a base-2 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)\n  a field: yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(2^2) = x mod f and gcd(x^(2^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)\n  check by brute force over all 4 x 4 products: every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add\n  x has order 3: the modulus is primitive\n  unit group: cyclic of order 3 = 3; phi(3) = 2 generators\n  subfields: GF(2), GF(2^2) (GF(2^d) for each d | 2: the a with a^(2^d) = a)\n  Frobenius a -> a^2: an automorphism of order 2 fixing GF(2); the Galois group is cyclic of order 2\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring GF(4)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "modulus": "the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 2 over GF(2) (by its coefficients read as a base-2 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)", "a_field": "yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(2^2) = x mod f and gcd(x^(2^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2)", "x_has_order_3": "the modulus is primitive", "unit_group": "cyclic of order 3 = 3; phi(3) = 2 generators", "subfields": "GF(2), GF(2^2) (GF(2^d) for each d | 2: the a with a^(2^d) = a)", "lhs": "GF(2^2)", "value": "GF(2)[x]/(x^2 + x + 1), 0x7", "headline": "GF(2^2) = GF(2)[x]/(x^2 + x + 1), 0x7", "details": ["4 elements (2^2), characteristic 2, dimension 2 over GF(2)", "Frobenius a -> a^2: an automorphism of order 2 fixing GF(2); the Galois group is cyclic of order 2"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity