{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "GF(3^2) = GF(3)[x]/(x^2 + x + 2)\n  9 elements (3^2), characteristic 3, dimension 2 over GF(3)\n  modulus: the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 2 over GF(3) (by its coefficients read as a base-3 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)\n  a field: yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(3^2) = x mod f and gcd(x^(3^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)\n  check by brute force over all 9 x 9 products: every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add\n  x has order 8: the modulus is primitive\n  unit group: cyclic of order 8 = 2^3; phi(8) = 4 generators\n  subfields: GF(3), GF(3^2) (GF(3^d) for each d | 2: the a with a^(3^d) = a)\n  Frobenius a -> a^3: an automorphism of order 2 fixing GF(3); the Galois group is cyclic of order 2\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring GF(3^2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "modulus": "the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 2 over GF(3) (by its coefficients read as a base-3 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)", "a_field": "yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(3^2) = x mod f and gcd(x^(3^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2)", "x_has_order_8": "the modulus is primitive", "unit_group": "cyclic of order 8 = 2^3; phi(8) = 4 generators", "subfields": "GF(3), GF(3^2) (GF(3^d) for each d | 2: the a with a^(3^d) = a)", "lhs": "GF(3^2)", "value": "GF(3)[x]/(x^2 + x + 2)", "headline": "GF(3^2) = GF(3)[x]/(x^2 + x + 2)", "details": ["9 elements (3^2), characteristic 3, dimension 2 over GF(3)", "Frobenius a -> a^3: an automorphism of order 2 fixing GF(3); the Galois group is cyclic of order 2"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)"}, {"kind": "by_brute_force_over_all_9_x_9_products", "passed": true, "text": "every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add"}], "files": [], "text": "GF(3^2) = GF(3)[x]/(x^2 + x + 2)\n  9 elements (3^2), characteristic 3, dimension 2 over GF(3)\n  modulus: the smallest primitive polynomial of degree 2 over GF(3) (by its coefficients read as a base-3 number; not necessarily the Conway polynomial)\n  a field: yes, the modulus is irreducible (Rabin: x^(3^2) = x mod f and gcd(x^(3^(2/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp's matrix has nullity 1 (one irreducible factor)\n  check by brute force over all 9 x 9 products: every nonzero element has an inverse, no zero divisors, commutative and equal to shift-and-add\n  x has order 8: the modulus is primitive\n  unit group: cyclic of order 8 = 2^3; phi(8) = 4 generators\n  subfields: GF(3), GF(3^2) (GF(3^d) for each d | 2: the a with a^(3^d) = a)\n  Frobenius a -> a^3: an automorphism of order 2 fixing GF(3); the Galois group is cyclic of order 2\n"}, "isError": false}}
